Late morning sweep October 30 2026, fired fifty-five minutes after the midday pass: three entries catalogued from the newest pages, and two of the six raw candidates turned out to be guides already shipped, which is the finding only a short window produces. Tuqui MCP - https://tuqui.com/mcp answered a keyless tools/list with 401 {"error":"unauthorized"}, the expected state for a connector bound to a vendor account; the card was filed on mcp.so 2026-10-21 with repository github.com/Tuqui-AI/tuqui-mcp (200), docs.tuqui.com (200) and LGPL-3.0, and the claim is the absence of a build, nothing installed in Odoo and one URL added to the assistant. Two sentences carry the review, read-only by default and only what your Odoo user can see, the second reusing Odoo's own per-user record rules rather than inventing a parallel permission model; versions 16 through 20 across Community, Enterprise, Odoo Online, Odoo.sh and self-hosted. The comparison against the catalogued Odoo server is not setup versus no setup because both claim little Odoo-side configuration: the local server takes ODOO_DB and ODOO_PASSWORD into your own config while this one holds the session vendor-side behind a consent screen, and the local server is generic by design while this one puts a skills layer for sales stock and collections in front of the ORM. Gap recorded: tools/list needs a token, so the tool count and write behaviour are the vendor's position and not a driven list. MarketPrint MCP - https://mcp.marketprint.de/mcp answered 401 with "Missing bearer token. Connect via OAuth, or use a static mcpacct_ token from your account settings", a refusal that names both credential paths and is therefore better than most; card filed 2026-10-14, vendor MarketConsultive GmbH, authType oauth, no repository because the service is closed. Production is split by destination, Germany for Europe and Houston Texas for the USA, which in print-on-demand decides whether a shipping estimate survives a customs form, so the destination belongs in the conversation as a field and not an inference. Four channels, Shopify Etsy WooCommerce and TikTok Shop, which are four commercial models wearing the same word listing. This is the catalogue's first print-on-demand entry and its first look at the supply side where a physical object begins to exist, and the failure mode is worse than a read: a bad publish costs a live listing with a wrong price attached to a product that will be manufactured. Gap recorded: the publish path is capable but unverified. Casus MCP - https://mcp.wearecasus.com/mcp answered 401 to a keyless tools/list and 405 to a bare GET, the normal pair for an OAuth-gated POST-only endpoint, and is flagged official on mcpservers.org at position 2 of the newest page. The corpus is deliberately national: 230,419 articles of 77 codes from Legifrance with successive versions, BOFiP administrative doctrine, more than 3.4 million court decisions by number or ECLI, tax treaties and EU law, as of 18 October 2026. The reason to care is the date axis: get_code_article reads an article in the version applicable to a given date and resolve_references grades a citation as found, found with a difference, ambiguous, not found, not applicable at the date or outside the corpus, statuses that are not a boolean and that an agent collapsing into not-found destroys. Two self-descriptions earn it, quoted not paraphrased: a text absent from the Casus corpus is not a text that does not exist, and the version history is partial reaching back mostly to 2025 so an earlier date can return undetermined at the date because the connector does not guess. Scope legal:read, one log line per tool call, semantic search passing through Voyage AI embeddings and a Pinecone index while other tools hit the corpus database directly. New slice: a national corpus with versioning and administrative doctrine attached, which neither the US retrieval entry nor the generic EU grounding entry covers. Gap recorded: tool names come from vendor documentation. Duplicates caught: free-seo-audit-for-claude on mcp.so /servers resolves to github.com/houtini-ai/seo-audit and @houtini/seo-audit-console 0.17.0 on npm, which is the catalogued SEO Audit Console MCP added 2026-10-28, missed by the slug cross-reference because the directory slug and guide directory share no full normalised form and settled by the repository plus npm record; best-ai-search-agency-aeo-report resolves to https://aeoengine.ai/mcp driven keyless to run_aeo_report and get_aeo_report_status, matching the catalogued AEO Engine MCP exactly. Held: three paid sponsorship cards arrived carrying utm_medium=paid_sponsorship, Fulcra Dynamics and Springbrand.ai both returning 404 on their detail pages so neither has a drivable surface and nothing is claimed, StockCake MCP on the design and media generation class; GPT Image Hub same class; FFxF unchanged from the midday hold an hour earlier; FSB (full-self-browsinhg, typo in the published slug) is DOM-first browser automation, MIT, github.com/fullselfbrowsing/FSB at 200, but createdAt 2025-02-23 makes it a year-old project newly indexed rather than an arrival, held on the browser automation class; Poker Bots All Stars is agent poker, consumer entertainment; kin and cli-a2b26f are generic slugs with nothing to evaluate; Anry and m1k3 were dispositioned 28 October morning and 18 October night. Counts: mcpservers.org counter 18,402, 27 unique entries on the newest page with 5 description-bearing TanStack blocks and 22 from the JSON-LD breadcrumb, both extractions needed because JSON-LD returned no names on this read and TanStack returned only 5 described blocks; guide tree 1,062 tracked server entries before this pass and 1,065 after, 1,182 guide files counting the legacy flat pages beside the directories.
